  "label": "User projected onto the visual material of the three survivors",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the three emaciated survivors, as the meme uses their suffering and historical context to evoke an emotional or critical response. The absence of explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you' means the projection is implicit — the user is invited to see themselves as a viewer of this traumatic historical moment, or to identify with the victims or the act of colorization. The projection is onto the visual material (three_individuals) which is central to the meme's hateful intent of trivializing Holocaust trauma.",
